```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Agent runtime builders (LangChain/LlamaIndex/custom loops) serving latency-bound workloads with fan-out patterns (parallel API calls, multi-source retrieval) who can guarantee dependency-detector false-negative rate ≤2.5%; narrowly applicable to platforms where ≥55% of steps have width≥2 (balanced mix) and correctness risk ≤5% is acceptable.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only for now. Constructed corpus (not tau-bench/AppWorld/BFCL traces) shows f_indep>30% across mixes (0.49–0.72) and 1.42× heterogeneous speedup at balanced mix, but Part B FAILED: at realistic detector error e=0.05, f_wrong≈10–12% (above 5% bar). The "free latency win" is NOT free; it trades wall-clock for correctness risk. Speedup is modest-to-moderate (1.14–1.69×) and strongly mix-dependent (19% exploitable steps in seq-heavy vs 85% in fan-out-heavy).
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Mechanism already shipped—LLMCompiler DAG dispatch, OpenAI/Anthropic native parallel tool calls, ReWOO, AsyncLM—so novelty is characterization, not product capability; Correctness risk 10–12% at e=0.05 exceeds production tolerance; Detector must achieve e≤0.025 (unproven on real traces—L1 open question); Speedup discounted by heterogeneous latencies (1.42× vs 1.72× ideal) and vanishes in seq-heavy workloads (1.14×); No validation on real agent benchmarks—mix, detector FN rate, and end-to-end correctness unmeasured]
RATIONALE: EXP-0014 Part A HELD (f_indep>0.30 across mixes, 0.442–0.713 in multi-call steps per results/metricA2_exploitable_parallelism.csv) but Part B FAILED at pre-registered threshold (f_wrong=0.103–0.123 at e=0.05 per results/metricB_fwrong_vs_detector_error.csv, vs ≤0.05 required). Exploitable parallelism is mix-conditional: frac steps width≥2 ranges 0.193 (pessimistic_seq_heavy) to 0.851 (optimistic_fanout), 0.550 at balanced_realistic. Heterogeneous-latency speedup is 1.14–1.69× (1.42× balanced) per results/metricC_latency_headroom.csv, not the 2×+ implied by "substantial wall-clock". Prior art (LLMCompiler, OpenAI/Anthropic parallel calls) already ships the mechanism; contribution is empirical characterization and f_wrong(e) bound, not a deployable product win. Negative result is actionable: establishes e≲0.025 target for ≤5% corruption, but L1 real-trace measurement is required to determine if any production detector meets it.
```
